"""Document the approved follow-up without applying the separate audit proposals."""
import update


def main():
    root=update.ROOT;w=update.load(update.WORLD);names=update.names()
    fn=update.replacer({**names,**update.FAMILIES})
    first=update.replacer({a.split()[0]:b.split()[0] for a,b in names.items()})
    path=root/'world-draft/Ardelis - Development Notes.md';text=first(fn(path.read_text(encoding='utf-8')))
    marker='## 5 November follow-up — current delivery\n'
    if marker in text:
        a=text.index(marker);b=text.index('## Scope and geography',a);text=text[:a]+text[b:]
    text=text.replace('The twelve incoming region coordinates, images and crops remain exact. The eighteen incoming local pins retain x/y and relative order through a recorded old-to-new name mapping. New pins are approximate placements for the author\'s adjustment. `tools/ardelis/placements.json` is the complete placement ledger; the companion landmark inventory separates visible-map interpretations from ordinary service additions.',
      'The later complete Locations and Regions exports supersede the initial provisional pins. All 391 locations and 55 regions match those normalized incoming sections exactly. The Ardelis grid remains four by three. All 84 Ardelis positions are now author-corrected; `tools/ardelis-followup/placements.json` and its CSV record their current values. The original placement ledger remains historical.')
    text=text.replace("Twenty-three new principals receive portraits first, including three paladin leaders. Vladimir receives one newly authorized portrait; the supporting cast's portraits are deferred as agreed.",
      'All 115 new Ardelis NPCs now have selected, officially uploaded portraits, including the three major paladins. Vladimir retains his approved replacement. There are 116 selected portraits in the complete archive.')
    a=text.index('**Delivery status:**');b=text.index('\n\n',a)
    text=text[:a]+('**Delivery status:** the current follow-up installs all 116 selected portrait URLs, preserves 84 location and two area images, and merges the author’s latest complete map sections. Exact files, names, targets and URLs are checked in `tools/ardelis-followup/art-verification.json`. Validation results and the completion status are recorded in CURRENT_STATE. This is an import package; it does not save or publish the Studio world.')+text[b:]
    insert=(marker+'\n'
      'Build on current Ardelis commit `1b42222`, not the earlier Rebirth export. `tools/ardelis-followup/review.json` is a reversible delta and historical fixtures reconstruct their original revisions without relaxing old assertions. Do not rerun the old builder or one-time migration against the current file.\n\n'
      '**Names and history:** 108 Ardelis character names and four associated family forms are migrated throughout native references. Shared human names reflect the former settlement’s heritage; western fantasy court dress and architecture remain. Noelle Ashford and five established Elven names stay unchanged. Glowhaven’s founders led independence after heavy imperial taxes and coerced mage war service; the empire formally recognizes the new nation while the crown retains an agenda. No founding date, battle roster or historical ruler is invented.\n\n'
      '**Focused progression repairs:** a genuinely resolved peaceful delegation can advance directly from phase 1 to 3 without forcing Vladimir into the scene. Genuine ongoing questioning and Shiba’s death retain separate paths. Carrier and audience leads now initialize only while the exact native quest is planned. Available, accepted, completed, rejected, abandoned and expired quests are not reinitialized. Existing XP and rewards remain owned by their original undertaking.\n\n'
      '**Recurring pursuit:** the actual player with both the Summoned one origin and corroborated trace is the bearer. After the initial interception or established phase-5 investigation, a suitable public scene may host a finite retrieval attempt. The controller requires at least 100 completed game ticks after the previous actual resolution, defers combat and protected/private venues, and never stacks an active attempt. Stronger spectators do not raise the bearer’s level band. One lead uses target level ±2 capped at 45; from the third attempt at most one weaker support may join, capped at 35. Desperation changes tactics rather than endlessly adding bodies.\n\n'
      'Native semantic conditions judge genuine scene suitability and an actual ended encounter; scripts own bearer identity, interval, team bounds and end flags. NPC generation still creates the requested new instances: their final stats and live scheduling need a Voyage test. Capture remains real captivity; the cooldown is not release or healing. The receiving-operation conclusion stops new teams without erasing current danger. Runtime lore contains setting facts; numeric implementation notes stay here and in the controllers.\n\n'
      '**Portrait selection:** supporting pose draws are recorded once. Jōji’s original was restored after an erroneous selection for replacement. The selected new passes are Maiko’s pose, Akito after rejection, Edmée’s angled pose, Kaede’s intact rapier and Rumi after rejection. Each has explicit author authorization and previous-selection provenance. Kaede’s later screenshot clarified the already selected replacement and did not authorize or produce another generation. Noelle’s previously approved choice remains. Some outputs have tighter headroom or prop encroachment than the guide, and repeated city-arch backgrounds; no automatic rerolls or quality claims conceal those limits.\n\n'
      '**Audit scope:** the Gemini DOCX was reviewed, with reproducible observations and unsupported claims separated in `research/Gemini Audit Review - 2026-11-05.md`. The author chose findings first. No scroll, guild-board, equipment-slot, opening-placement, encounter-guidance or travel-toggle repair from that audit is included. `audit_snapshot.cjs` is diagnostic only.\n\n'
      '**Verification:** `test_ardelis_followup.cjs` covers the incoming section hashes, name/reference migration, preserved Spider content and party diadem, peaceful transition, guarded offers, same-bearer selection, 100-turn pacing, scene guards, count/caps and concluded-operation stop. These are static and isolated emitted-script tests; they do not prove live semantic judgment, generated stats or multiplayer scheduling. Playtest peaceful departure, optional investigation order, actual pursuit escape/capture, a mixed party and final stop before release.\n\n')
    text=text.replace('## Scope and geography',insert+'## Scope and geography',1)
    path.write_text(text,encoding='utf-8')
    # Current map handoff is reconstructed only from the incoming native records.
    regions=sorted([(k,v) for k,v in w['regions'].items() if v.get('realm')=='Ardelis'],key=lambda p:(-p[1]['y'],p[1]['x']))
    pins=update.load(update.HERE/'placements.json')
    lines=['# Ardelis map and landmark handoff','','Current geometry: author-corrected complete Studio exports supplied on 5 November. These supersede the initial 18 pinned sites and 66 approximate additions. The map remains four columns by three rows; each location’s local x/y differs from its region’s grid x/y. No tile or pin is inferred anew from the master PNG.','','All 84 Ardelis locations use the supplied corrected positions, region memberships, images and crops. Twenty Glowhaven region map URLs from the same incoming Regions export are also retained. Name normalization only substitutes approved character/house aliases; region order and local coordinates are preserved.','','## Current region grid','','| Region | Grid x | Grid y |','|---|---:|---:|']
    lines += [f"| {n} | {r['x']} | {r['y']} |" for n,r in regions]
    lines += ['','## Complete current pins','','The label “author-corrected” records provenance, not a claim that every illustrated roof was independently recognized. The eighteen initial placeholder names remain in the source column of the placement CSV.','']
    for n,r in regions:
        lines += ['### '+n,'','| Location | Local x | Local y |','|---|---:|---:|']
        for p in pins:
            if p['region']==n:lines.append(f"| {p['name']} | {p['x']} | {p['y']} |")
        lines.append('')
    lines += ['## Landmark interpretation and interiors','','Visible map features informed the archive complex, aqueduct, reservoir, western amphitheatre and exercise field, northeastern observatory and crystal works, southwestern mills, eastern locks and small harbor tower. Their functions and ownership are authored choices. Markets, lodging, trades, homes and public services fill existing city fabric rather than requiring giant new map buildings.','','The palace descent remains connected areas inside Caelrath Palace. The separate sewer site is in its current supplied region and never creates a free palace shortcut. The portal room has a separate area establishing shot. Thaurivex and other named actors are not permanently painted into static location images.','','Current placement source: `tools/ardelis-followup/placements.json` and `placements.csv`. Initial `tools/ardelis/` pin records remain historical.']
    (root/'world-draft/Ardelis - Map and Landmark Handoff.md').write_text('\n'.join(lines)+'\n',encoding='utf-8')
    path=root/'world-draft/Ardelis - Patch Notes.md';text=path.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
    text=text.replace('Principal characters receive new portraits, and the capital gains location artwork inspired by its distinctive map.',
      'The entire new cast receives portraits, from the royal household to working residents and guild regulars. The capital also gains location artwork inspired by its distinctive map.')
    phrase='Vladimir can help arrange a passage, but the independent court route remains open.'
    text=text.replace(phrase,phrase+' Unresolved imperial business can bring occasional retrieval attempts after your mana trail is genuinely identified. Defeating a team may buy time without ending the operation behind it.')
    text=text.replace('Lore now reaches further into the empire’s faith, politics, households and ordinary life',
      'Lore now reaches further into the empire’s faith, politics, households, shared history with independent Glowhaven and ordinary life')
    path.write_text(text,encoding='utf-8')
    decisions=root/'docs/DECISIONS.md';text=decisions.read_text(encoding='utf-8')
    if '## 5 November — Ardelis complete-cast follow-up' not in text:
        text+='\n\n## 5 November — Ardelis complete-cast follow-up\n\n'
        text+='The author approves Japanese-inspired human naming across Ardelis and Glowhaven, retaining Noelle Ashford, French Elven names and heritage-appropriate Dwarven names. Glowhaven began as an imperial-backed settlement; heavy taxation and forced mage war service led the four archmage founders to independence. Ardelis formally recognizes the new nation, while its crown remains resentful. Preserve western fantasy clothing and architecture.\n\n'
        text+='Merge the latest complete Locations/Regions exports exactly after approved aliases. Finish all supporting portraits and upload only each selected exact name/hash; preserve the approved majors. Explicit portrait corrections cover Maiko, Akito, Edmée, Kaede and Rumi. Jōji is restored to the original. The later Kaede screenshot is clarification, not another generation. No automatic rerolls.\n\n'
        text+='Repair the genuine peaceful-departure gap and guard duplicate investigation quest offers. Keep the Spider anomaly and party-wide diadem. Add recurring pursuit of the actually traced Summoned one, scaled to that bearer with finite opposition, at least 100 completed ticks after the last actual resolution, scene-aware deferral and a campaign conclusion stop. Semantic outcomes remain native; exact ownership and pacing remain script checks.\n\n'
        text+='The Gemini report is audit findings first, per explicit answer. Record real defects, incorrect schema claims and untested hypotheses separately. Do not apply its scroll, board, item-slot, placement or other proposed repairs, or change encounter rules/travel settings, in this update.\n'
        decisions.write_text(text,encoding='utf-8')


if __name__=='__main__':main()
